  "sn22.55:8.8": "",
  "sn22.55:8.9": "“Will vanish” is <i lang='pi' translate='no'>vibhavissati</i>, literally “will cease to be”, the verbal form of the word “nonexistence” (<i lang='pi' translate='no'>vibhava</i>) in the second noble truth. It’s used throughout <a href='https://suttacentral.net/snp4.11/en/sujato'>Snp 4.11</a> and, in a meditation context, in <a href='https://suttacentral.net/an11.9/en/sujato#7.1'>AN 11.9:7.1</a>. At <a href='https://suttacentral.net/iti49/en/sujato#7.3'>Iti 49:7.3</a> it refers to the ending of continued existence for an arahant. ",
  "sn22.55:8.10": "",
